-- title:
--   Cyclotomic ramification over a complete coefficient ring, all primes
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is $(q)$, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain that is an $A_0$-algebra, finite as an $A_0$-module, with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A_0\,A$ injective; assume $A$ contains an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity and that $A_0[\zeta] = A$ (the $A_0$-subalgebra generated by $\{\zeta\}$ is $\top$), and let $\varpi\in A$ satisfy $\mathfrak m_A = (\varpi)$. Let $W_0$ be a discrete valuation domain, complete with respect to its maximal ideal, which is an $A_0$-algebra and satisfies $\mathfrak m_{W_0} = (q)$. Let $R_0$ be a local ring which is a $W_0$-algebra via a local homomorphism, and let $\sigma_0 : A \to R_0$ be a ring homomorphism agreeing on $A_0$ with $A_0 \to W_0 \to R_0$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $W_1$ carrying a commutative ring structure making it a discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal ideal, together with ring homomorphisms $j_1 : W_0 \to W_1$, $\sigma : A \to W_1$ and a local homomorphism $\iota_1 : W_1 \to R_0$, such that $j_1$ followed by $\iota_1$ is the structure map $W_0 \to R_0$, $\sigma$ followed by $\iota_1$ is $\sigma_0$, $\sigma(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A_0\,A\,a_0) = j_1(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A_0\,W_0\,a_0)$ for all $a_0\in A_0$, $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma\varpi)$, and $(\sigma\varpi)^{q-1} = \varepsilon_1\, q$ in $W_1$ for some unit $\varepsilon_1$.
--
--   This is the construction of the totally ramified cyclotomic extension $W_1 = W_0[\zeta_q]$ of a complete coefficient ring, Eisenstein of degree $q-1$ over $W_0$, in a form compatible with a prescribed local target $R_0$; the present version removes the restriction $q \ge 3$ and so covers all primes. It is used in the construction of coefficient rings for supersingular stalk charts on modular curves of full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsPrimitiveRoot_exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_isAdicComplete_ringHom_comp_eq_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pow_sub_one_eq_mul_of_adjoin_eq_top_of_prime.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
